		summary = "**Muthuswami Dikshitar** (24 March 1776–21 October 1835; also known as **Mudduswamy Dikshitar** and, mononymously, as **Dikshitar**, and sometimes **Guruguha**), was a South Indian Hindu poet, singer, veena player, and prolific composer of [[Indian classical music]]. He was the youngest member of the Trinity of Carnatic music, alongside [[Tyagaraja]] (1767–1847), and [[Syama Sastri]] (1762–1827).",
